  "content": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Previously, I restricted rm and checked who entered commands and whether they were blocked. This time I reopened the terminal screen from that work."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Selecting a session in Session Logs replayed the connection screen and output. I could jump to the blocked deletion and later file checks. Command Audit’s direct link to the relevant recording time was particularly useful."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Finding the Completed Session"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "In Audit → Servers → Session Logs, Demo Developer returned the two earlier SSH sessions with user, role, account, and server."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
